# 005 · A sample project in `examples/`

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

Put a small sample project and its kit in `examples/`, starting with the matrix-multiply project that the smoke check uses. A contract and the New campaign page can then name a folder inside a repository, so a tester points a campaign at this repository and `examples/<name>`. The quick start runs a first agent campaign on it.

## Why

Today a project must be a whole repository at an https or ssh git URL. A tester with no project of their own cannot run agents.

## Done when

- [ ] `examples/` holds at least one project with its kit and a short README.
- [ ] A contract's project can name a folder in a repository. The rig fetches the repository and uses that folder as the project's root.
- [ ] New campaign offers the folder field, with a description.
- [ ] The quick start runs a first agent campaign on the sample, with a free model, to a first verdict.
- [ ] The campaign acceptance covers a project in a folder.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: The sample lives in this repository under `examples/`, not in a separate repository.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.

